WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.533 --> 00:00:01.801 line:7%
[russian speech]

00:00:03.302 --> 00:00:06.539 line:0%
- There were many tense moments,
and according to state media,

00:00:06.639 --> 00:00:10.610 line:0%
hundreds of arrests
made in Moscow alone.

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:14.214
Our crew also getting caught
up in the pushing and shoving.

00:00:14.314 --> 00:00:16.149 line:0%
There's a massive
police presence on hand

00:00:16.249 --> 00:00:17.350 line:7%
here at these protests.

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:20.119 line:0%
And time and again, we're
seeing scenes like this,

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:23.323 line:0%
with the police pushing
and even making arrests.

00:00:23.423 --> 00:00:24.457
OK.
OK.

00:00:24.557 --> 00:00:25.424
OK.
OK.

00:00:25.524 --> 00:00:26.225
OK.

00:00:26.325 --> 00:00:27.827
OK.

00:00:27.927 --> 00:00:30.262
[russian speech]

00:00:30.363 --> 00:00:32.298
Russia's official news
agency put the turnout

00:00:32.398 --> 00:00:35.901
at around 8,000 people at
the march in Moscow, declared

00:00:36.001 --> 00:00:39.472
illegal by Russian authorities.

00:00:39.572 --> 00:00:41.741
Taking to the streets to
criticize what they called

00:00:41.841 --> 00:00:44.577
widespread corruption
among the country's elite,

00:00:44.677 --> 00:00:46.612
the organizers say
similar gatherings

00:00:46.712 --> 00:00:49.348
happened in about
100 towns and cities

00:00:49.448 --> 00:00:51.651
across this vast country.

00:00:51.751 --> 00:00:53.619
The man calling for
the action, opposition

00:00:53.719 --> 00:00:56.155
activist and Kremlin
critic, Alexei Navalny,

00:00:56.255 --> 00:00:57.157
was himself detained.

00:00:59.926 --> 00:01:01.894
But those who followed
his call weren't

00:01:01.994 --> 00:01:03.896
shy to voice their grievances.

00:01:03.996 --> 00:01:05.231
- I'm against Putin.

00:01:05.331 --> 00:01:06.499
Against his corruption.

00:01:06.599 --> 00:01:09.835
- They can't support our
governments with their greed.

00:01:09.935 --> 00:01:16.575
They steal out money
by using their power.

00:01:16.676 --> 00:01:18.944
- These protests still
pose a serious threat

00:01:19.044 --> 00:01:21.480
to Russia's president
Vladimir Putin, who boasts

00:01:21.580 --> 00:01:24.984
approval ratings of around 80%.

00:01:25.084 --> 00:01:26.819
But they showed
that the opposition

00:01:26.919 --> 00:01:28.887
is willing to take
to the streets

00:01:28.988 --> 00:01:31.423
whether the authorities
allow them to or not.

00:01:31.523 --> 00:01:33.256
Fred Pleitgen, CNN Moscow.

